Z||000000||Daleford||12-09-2001||06:50 PM||||Since I will be ending up with a 115 mm bolt circle on the rear of a kit/Fiero chassis, I would like to have the same bolt circle up front.  I notice the Pontiac 6000 has the same bolt circle as the Fiero, [100mm] but... the 6000 HD., STE., and diesel have 115mm.<BR>Any way of attaching these spindles, etc to the front of an 86 Fiero?    Thanks<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||AnimalGT||12-10-2001||03:54 AM||||Look at Held Motorsports web site (I don't have the address handy).  They make a drop spindle kit that uses the Fiero rear hub assemblies on the front spindles.  The 6000HD hub assys. will work on these too.  I have been considering doing the 115mm conversion myself.<BR>Scott ||||reg||1
